Elisp written for GNU Emacs 24 and later reaches for a few things XEmacs
never grew: eval with a LEXICAL argument, defvar-local, alist-get,
string-trim, string-empty-p, and delete-dups on 21.4.  This package
defines each of them only when it is missing, so a package that needs
them can require xemacs-compat and keep the same sources it uses
everywhere else.
